    "narrative": "The Zurich Zebras enter today\u2019s slate with **Pete Crow-Armstrong** (80.98) headlining our lineup. He is the clear top play, buoyed by a favorable matchup against Andre Pallante and a high-probability SB environment; the combination of a slow pitcher delivery and a premium leadoff spot makes him an elite engine for our category scarcity needs. Joining him in the \"Strong\" tier are **Junior Caminero** (72.75) and **Yordan Alvarez** (71.46). **Junior Caminero** benefits significantly from the matchup against Walbert Ure\u00f1a, while **Yordan Alvarez** remains locked in due to his elite 0.425 xwOBA, proving that his raw production remains a necessity even without the high-end speed upside of our other leadoff men. **Colt Keith** (68.51) also earns a high score today, as the matchup against Erick Fedde provides a rare dual benefit of a weak starter and an increased stolen base opportunity.\n\nThe most difficult roster decision today was excluding **Chase Meidroth** (53.47). While his metrics against the struggling Troy Melton were robust\u2014particularly the SP skill advantage\u2014the optimizer ultimately preferred the higher raw power ceilings of **Luke Raley** and **Carson Benge** in the lower-scoring slots. We also flagged **Hyeseong Kim** as a high-risk hold; despite his elite speed, the brutal matchup against Zack Wheeler and the negative impact of his low lineup position rendered him a liability for a 5x5 Roto effort today. Looking at situational drivers, **Kazuma Okamoto** (66.27) received a +16% park adjustment that vaulted him into the starting rotation, providing a significant boost to our batting average floor.\n\nAll current evaluations are subject to volatility as we wait on official lineup confirmations for **Gary Sanchez**, **Dillon Dingler**, **Luke Raley**, and others. Be advised that while we are targeting SB upside with **Trea Turner** (63.25) and **Kyle Schwarber** (61.14)\u2014both of whom benefit from positive wind conditions\u2014the SP skill variance against Justin Wrobleski introduces moderate risk. We will monitor the weather in the **Kyle Schwarber** game closely, as the wind-out boost is contingent on current atmospheric forecasts holding through first pitch. With **Zac Veen** still confirmed in the minors, our roster remains static for this turn.",
